# CODEOWNERS — review routing for the Shadow Engine.
#
# Each line maps a path pattern to the reviewer(s) responsible for it. The
# LAST matching pattern wins, so specific areas below override the catch-all
# `*`. Teams use @org/team; individuals use @username.
#
# Every @handle referenced below must be declared in the MAINTAINERS file at
# the repo root (the canonical GitHub handle list) - `make check-github`
# enforces this so review routing can never point at a misspelled or made-up
# account. To add a maintainer, list their real handle in MAINTAINERS first,
# then assign them per-area below, e.g.
#   /Games/   @godofecht/games-team
#   /Engine/  @username2

# Catch-all: anything not covered by a more specific rule below.
*                       @godofecht

# Engine core — gameplay framework, rendering, ECS, physics bindings.
/Engine/                @godofecht

# The 100-game program and the example demos.
/Games/                 @godofecht
/Examples/              @godofecht

# Unit suite — the coverage gate depends on these staying in sync with code.
/tests/                 @godofecht

# CI, build, and repo tooling — workflows, gates, sanitizers, valgrind.
/.github/               @godofecht
/cmake/                 @godofecht
/tools/                 @godofecht
/CMakeLists.txt         @godofecht
/Makefile               @godofecht
/build_wasm.sh          @godofecht
/*.sh                   @godofecht

# Docs — the check-docs gate keeps these recipes tied to the Makefile.
/*.md                   @godofecht
